  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31404494",
      "title": "Fetching Backend Data (GET Requests)",
      "lectureOrder": 164,
      "videoOrder": 160,
      "sourceHash": "e00f140f82b4e76935ad9fb202a1d88772757273270c79a288a063d7784e8e4d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 4.25,
          "en": "So as a next step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.25,
          "end": 7.65,
          "en": "let's fetch some data from the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.65,
          "end": 10.58,
          "en": "And for this, we can add another utility function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.58,
          "end": 12.77,
          "en": "in http.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.77,
          "end": 16.88,
          "en": "and maybe name it fetchExpenses or getExpenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.51,
          "end": 21.52,
          "en": "The name of course is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.52,
          "end": 24.89,
          "en": "Export it to make it available outside of this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.89,
          "end": 27.89,
          "en": "And now, we want to set a get request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.89,
          "end": 30.063,
          "en": "by using Axios get method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.17,
          "end": 33.82,
          "en": "Now, the URL to which we sent the request",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.82,
          "end": 36.16,
          "en": "should be the same URL as here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 36.16,
          "end": 38.59,
          "en": "where we actually stored an expense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.59,
          "end": 40.84,
          "en": "because we wanna get all those expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.84,
          "end": 43.31,
          "en": "So the URL is the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.31,
          "end": 46.55,
          "en": "But with that, we already got some copy and pasting going on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 46.55,
          "end": 49.13,
          "en": "and we got this long URL everywhere.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 49.13,
          "end": 50.86,
          "en": "And if we ever need to change it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.86,
          "end": 53.66,
          "en": "for example, to switch from a development backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.66,
          "end": 55.02,
          "en": "to a production backend,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 55.02,
          "end": 57.18,
          "en": "we need to change it in multiple places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.18,
          "end": 59.423,
          "en": "at least the start of the URL.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.29,
          "end": 63.37,
          "en": "And therefore, I will actually add a little constant here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.37,
          "end": 66.77,
          "en": "the BACKEND_URL constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.77,
          "end": 71.2,
          "en": "where I wanna store this URL root, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.69,
          "end": 77.4,
          "en": "and then here we can construct the string dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.4,
          "end": 79.8,
          "en": "by using BACKEND_URL +,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 79.8,
          "end": 82.09,
          "en": "and then just change the path at the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.09,
          "end": 83.7,
          "en": "because that path at the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.7,
          "end": 86.93,
          "en": "might be different for different types of requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.93,
          "end": 88.39,
          "en": "even though it is the same here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.39,
          "end": 90.46000000000001,
          "en": "But later, we will send other requests",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.46000000000001,
          "end": 92.963,
          "en": "where this path at the end will be different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.2,
          "end": 97.15,
          "en": "But with that, we now manage this in a central place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.15,
          "end": 101.58,
          "en": "And we're now sending this get request to get our expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.58,
          "end": 104.19,
          "en": "Get doesn't need a second argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 106.05,
          "en": "we could pass extra config,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.05,
          "end": 108.22,
          "en": "but we don't need to pass any data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.22,
          "end": 109.75999999999999,
          "en": "because we we're not sending any data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 109.75999999999999,
          "end": 110.96000000000001,
          "en": "we're just getting data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.12,
          "end": 114.86,
          "en": "Now, fetchExpenses can be called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 114.86,
          "end": 116.75999999999999,
          "en": "in RecentExpenses for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 116.75999999999999,
          "end": 120.223,
          "en": "because that is where we wanna get our expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 121.33,
          "end": 122.84,
          "en": "Now, to call it there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 122.84,
          "end": 124.47,
          "en": "we can use useEffect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 124.47,
          "end": 127.69,
          "en": "because that allows us to execute some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.69,
          "end": 129.24,
          "en": "that should execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 129.24,
          "end": 132.253,
          "en": "whenever the component re-renders, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.2,
          "end": 137.473,
          "en": "So here we can use useEffect in RecentExpenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 138.82,
          "end": 141.963,
          "en": "and of course also import this hook therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 143.56,
          "end": 146.853,
          "en": "And in useEffect, in this effect function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.77,
          "end": 150.07,
          "en": "we can call fetchExpenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 151.13,
          "end": 153.74,
          "en": "Of course, for that, you must import this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 153.74,
          "end": 156.39,
          "en": "and then it can be executed here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 156.39,
          "end": 159.3,
          "en": "However, now we're facing a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 159.3,
          "end": 163.79,
          "en": "Sending an http request is an asynchronous task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.79,
          "end": 167.2,
          "en": "That means it doesn't complete immediately.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 167.2,
          "end": 171.86,
          "en": "That's why post and get return promises.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 171.86,
          "end": 173.75,
          "en": "Now you should know what promises are,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 173.75,
          "end": 176.86,
          "en": "it's not React Native-specific, it's a JavaScript concept.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 176.86,
          "end": 180.66,
          "en": "Definitely explore dedicated JavaScript resources,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.66,
          "end": 183.5,
          "en": "like My JavaScript, The Complete Guide Course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.5,
          "end": 185.5,
          "en": "if you don't know what promises are,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 185.5,
          "end": 188.44,
          "en": "and if you don't have these fundamentals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.44,
          "end": 191.05,
          "en": "In short, a promise is an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 191.05,
          "end": 195.51,
          "en": "that will eventually give you access to some other data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.51,
          "end": 197.23,
          "en": "And here, get, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 197.23,
          "end": 200.2,
          "en": "will eventually give us access to the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 200.2,
          "end": 201.53300000000002,
          "en": "fetched from the backend.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 202.47,
          "end": 203.97,
          "en": "Now, to work with promises,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 203.97,
          "end": 207.01,
          "en": "we can add then on the promise object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 207.01,
          "end": 208.73,
          "en": "and then pass a function to then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 208.73,
          "end": 212.32999999999998,
          "en": "which will be called once the eventual data is there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 212.32999999999998,
          "end": 215.74,
          "en": "Or alternatively, we can use async await,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 215.74,
          "end": 218.75,
          "en": "which is a more modern JavaScript feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 218.75,
          "end": 221.01,
          "en": "And that is what I will use here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 221.01,
          "end": 224.12,
          "en": "I will turn this into a async function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 224.12,
          "end": 226.22,
          "en": "and then we can await this promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 226.22,
          "end": 229.01,
          "en": "and store the eventually returned data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 229.01,
          "end": 231.49,
          "en": "which in this case will be a response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 231.49,
          "end": 234.883,
          "en": "with more details about the response in a constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 235.74,
          "end": 238.27,
          "en": "So that's how we can use async await here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 238.27,
          "end": 241.11,
          "en": "and then the next line will only execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 241.11,
          "end": 242.69,
          "en": "once the response is there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 242.69,
          "end": 245.42,
          "en": "so once we have the response from the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 245.42,
          "end": 247.86,
          "en": "and then we can use this response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 247.86,
          "end": 250.28,
          "en": "Now, when it comes to using the response,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 250.28,
          "end": 253.3,
          "en": "for Firebase, the response we get back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 253.3,
          "end": 255.97,
          "en": "will actually be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 255.97,
          "end": 259.13,
          "en": "where these unique IDs will be keys,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 259.13,
          "end": 262.12,
          "en": "so property names in that object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 262.12,
          "end": 263.82,
          "en": "and if we had multiple expenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 263.82,
          "end": 268.04,
          "en": "we would have multiple property names that have this format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 268.04,
          "end": 270.04,
          "en": "And then we would have nested objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 270.04,
          "end": 272.78,
          "en": "for these keys, for these unique IDs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 272.78,
          "end": 274.89300000000003,
          "en": "that hold the actual data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 276.03,
          "end": 278,
          "en": "And I wanna transform that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 278,
          "end": 280.07,
          "en": "into an array of objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 280.07,
          "end": 283.59000000000003,
          "en": "where every object has the ID in an ID field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 283.59000000000003,
          "end": 285.407,
          "en": "and the amount, date and description",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 285.407,
          "end": 287.96,
          "en": "in other separate fields.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 287.96,
          "end": 291.11,
          "en": "For this, we can create an expenses helper constant,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 291.11,
          "end": 292.84000000000003,
          "en": "which holds an array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 292.84000000000003,
          "end": 294.09000000000003,
          "en": "and we can use a for loop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 294.09000000000003,
          "end": 298.35,
          "en": "to go through all our response keys.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 298.35,
          "end": 302.62,
          "en": "So we can go for all the keys in response.data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 302.62,
          "end": 306.7,
          "en": "Axios gives a as a data property on this response object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 306.7,
          "end": 308.29,
          "en": "which holds the actual data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 308.29,
          "end": 310.64300000000003,
          "en": "that was sent back by the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 311.72,
          "end": 314.76,
          "en": "So now we go through all the keys in that object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 314.76,
          "end": 318.12,
          "en": "because, as I just said, we will get back an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 318.12,
          "end": 321.223,
          "en": "And those keys will therefore be those IDs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 322.8,
          "end": 325.2,
          "en": "Now, for every key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 325.2,
          "end": 328.37,
          "en": "I wanna create a new expense object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 328.37,
          "end": 331.21,
          "en": "which should be an object, a JavaScript object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 331.21,
          "end": 333.253,
          "en": "that has an ID field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 334.13,
          "end": 336.273,
          "en": "which is that key I got here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 337.39,
          "end": 339.85,
          "en": "and that also has an amount field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 339.85,
          "end": 341.8,
          "en": "which is response.data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 343.27,
          "end": 345.653,
          "en": "for the given key.amount.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 346.75,
          "end": 348.54,
          "en": "I also want to set my date field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 348.54,
          "end": 353.01,
          "en": "which should be response.data Key.date.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 355.57,
          "end": 360.01,
          "en": "And I want to set my description field here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 360.01,
          "end": 364.513,
          "en": "to response.data Key.description.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 366.12,
          "end": 367.81,
          "en": "Now, this syntax here simply means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 367.81,
          "end": 370.49,
          "en": "that we dynamically access a property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 370.49,
          "end": 373.323,
          "en": "which name is stored in that key constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 374.4,
          "end": 378.8,
          "en": "So we access these different IDs, basically, in our data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 378.8,
          "end": 382.32,
          "en": "So in that object that is returned by Firebase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 382.32,
          "end": 384.89,
          "en": "And then we dive into amount, date, and description,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 384.89,
          "end": 388.873,
          "en": "to get that data and store it in our own equally named keys.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 389.72,
          "end": 392.64,
          "en": "Now I wanna transform the date to a date object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 392.64,
          "end": 395.23,
          "en": "by passing it to the date constructor,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 395.23,
          "end": 397.65,
          "en": "because Firebase stores the date as a string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 397.65,
          "end": 400.62,
          "en": "and I wanna convert it back into a date object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
